❯ I want to add a narrow-terminal
  regression check for wrapped prompt
  suggestions and multiline drafts.
  First, explain in one sentence why
  terminal width matters. I will ask
  you to outline the regression cases
  next.

● Terminal width matters because a
  narrow terminal forces long prompt
  suggestions and multiline drafts to
  soft-wrap across several rows, so any
  logic that reads the composer's
  contents by screen line (rather than
  by logical text) can misjudge a
  wrapped suggestion as real typed
  input, or a wrapped draft as empty or
  partial.

  Ready for the regression cases
  whenever you are.

